    [BugFix][KVPool] Recover ordinary layerwise pool transfer failures (#18812)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    GVA layerwise transfer threads currently raise on nonzero
    copy/write-completion return codes even when the pool is only an
    optional cache. A transient pool failure can therefore become a fatal
    worker error.
    
    - Make ordinary layerwise pool saves best-effort while preserving failed
    copy results in `batch_write_finish` and completing the existing
    request/event bookkeeping.
    - Report failed ordinary single-group pool loads through the existing
    invalid-block recovery path.
    - Keep strict errors for layer-reused offload and multi-group loads.
    Backend-raised exceptions and malformed write-completion responses
    remain strict.
    
    The existing metadata guard disables saving a request in the same
    forward pass that loads its pool KV; this change keeps that guard
    unchanged.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Nonzero GVA transfer return codes no longer terminate ordinary
    layerwise pool workers. Failed loads still follow the configured
    `kv_load_failure_policy` (for example, recomputation when configured).
    Layerwise offload behavior is unchanged. No configuration or environment
    variables are added.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Added regression tests for recoverable versus strict load/save failures,
    copy/write-completion failures, invalid-block reporting, and
    queue/event/request completion. Existing metadata tests cover load/save
    suppression.
    
    ```bash
    pytest -q tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_kv_transfer.py \
      tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store/test_metadata.py \
      --confcutdir=tests/ut/distributed/ascend_store
    # 128 passed, 47 subtests passed
    
    bash format.sh ci
    # All checks passed
    ```
    
    Tests ran with the repository's mocked dependencies on CPU. Full
    runtime/NPU integration tests and performance benchmarks were not run;
    hardware validation remains outstanding.
    
    ---
    
    ### Checklist
    
    #### Testing
    
    - [x] **Boundary / edge-case coverage**: Reviewed failure/success and
    strict/recoverable policy boundaries; no tensor-shape or sequence-length
    logic changes.
    - [x] **Regression test**: Added tests that fail without this fix.
    - [x] **Error / failure path coverage**: Covered nonzero copy and
    write-completion results.
    - [x] **Meaningful & reliable tests**: Assert invalid blocks, backend
    completion inputs, queue accounting, events, and finished requests.
    - [ ] **Performance impact**: No NPU benchmark available; no new device
    synchronization or copy operation is introduced.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
